# Exp. 1 (c) c_fjord3d -- case ${case}
# PD3 option (iii): RBCS imposes the plume-outflow T/S in the outflow cells
# only. rbcs_mask = q tau/V there (0 elsewhere), so the RBCS tendency
# -(mask/tau)(theta - T_out) (pkg/rbcs/rbcs_add_tendency.F:88-111) equals
# q (T_out - theta)/V, the source-at-T_out term addMass would add
# (apply_forcing.F:509-513); verified in the PD3 spike to 7e-5 degC.
# SHELF RELAXATION ZONE (task-7 round 2): the 10 columns west of the OB u-point
# (0-based nx-2-isl, isl = 1..10) relax T/S toward the time-varying shelf profile
# (the OBEt/OBEs record of the same time) with the mask of
# gendata.make_case.sponge_zone_mask = the former non-linear OBCS sponge
# (obcs_sponge.F:540-565) written as an RBCS tendency. Shelf records:
# rbcsForcingPeriod = externForcingPeriod, rbcsForcingCycle = externForcingCycle,
# rbcsForcingOffset = 0 (default): rbcs_fields_load.F:72-76 calls the same
# GET_PERIODIC_INTERVAL as obcs_fields_load.F:105 with time - offset, so record
# r sits at (r-1/2) period like OBEt. startTime=0 < 0.5 period only triggers a
# WARNING (rbcs_readparms.F:202-209), the interpolation still wraps to the last
# record. Cases without shelf forcing (shelf_amp = 0) also get the zone, relaxing
# to the constant initial profile (as the old sponge did). Cases without plume
# have no outflow cells.
 &RBCS_PARM01
 useRBCtemp=.TRUE.,
 useRBCsalt=.TRUE.,
 tauRelaxT=${rbcs_tau},
 tauRelaxS=${rbcs_tau},
 relaxMaskFile(1)='rbcs_mask.bin',
 relaxMaskFile(2)='rbcs_mask.bin',
 relaxTFile='rbcs_T.bin',
 relaxSFile='rbcs_S.bin',
 rbcsForcingPeriod=${externForcingPeriod},
 rbcsForcingCycle=${externForcingCycle},
 &
 &RBCS_PARM02
 &
